# Generated from: specs/bug-scope-cumulative-feature-specs-to-the-active-issue/requirements.md
# Issue: #162
# Type: Defect regression

@regression @issue-162 @issue-scope
Feature: Cumulative feature specs are scoped to the active issue
  Cumulative specs previously identified contributing issues without assigning
  individual completion units. Every lifecycle consumer must use one validated
  active delivery slice and explicit regression obligations.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Record machine-readable ownership and adoption
    Given multiple issues contribute acceptance criteria, functional requirements, tasks, and scenarios to one feature spec
    When write-spec accepts a new creation or amendment
    Then issue-scope.json assigns every element one owner
    And the active issue separately records any explicitly adopted existing elements
    And the resulting manifest validates against the cumulative spec inventory

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Implement only the active mapped slice
    Given earlier, active, adopted, and future tasks coexist in one cumulative tasks document
    When write-code resolves scope for the active issue
    Then its plan contains only the active issue's owned and adopted tasks
    And it does not execute earlier completed or future issue tasks

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Resume only incomplete tasks in the same active slice
    Given one mapped active task is complete and another mapped active task remains incomplete
    And unrelated cumulative tasks also exist
    When write-code reconstructs implementation progress
    Then it enumerates only the incomplete task from the active mapped slice
    And unrelated tasks cannot enter the resumed plan

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Separate current delivery verification from prior regression evidence
    Given the active issue maps current delivery elements and explicit prior regression contracts
    When verify-code evaluates the implementation
    Then current delivery ACs tasks and scenarios determine active completion
    And only declared prior ACs FRs and scenarios are evaluated as regression evidence
    And future or undeclared elements are excluded from the completion claim

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Bind reports and lifecycle status to the active mapping
    Given several issues share one canonical spec directory
    When verification and status artifacts are generated for the active issue
    Then both identify the active issue and the same normalized delivery and regression IDs
    And evidence for another issue cannot advance the active lifecycle stage

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Prepare an issue-scoped pull request
    Given the cumulative spec has a valid active issue scope
    When open-pr assembles spec-linked delivery content
    Then its summary acceptance criteria and test plan use only active delivery plus declared regression evidence
    And it links issue-scope.json
    And it closes only the active issue

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Fail safely when cumulative legacy ownership is ambiguous
    Given a multi-issue feature spec lacks a complete valid issue-scope manifest
    When any lifecycle consumer attempts to resolve the active issue
    Then the resolver returns repair_required with exact gaps
    And the consumer directs explicit repair through write-spec
    And it does not fall back to the whole cumulative spec

  @SCN008 @regression
  Scenario: Prove isolation with a cumulative lifecycle fixture
    Given a committed fixture contains earlier complete active owned active adopted regression and future elements
    When the resolver and every affected lifecycle contract are exercised for the active issue
    Then implementation resumption verification reporting status and pull-request preparation use the same isolated slice
    And deterministic tests reject cross-issue completion evidence
